WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.814
Staff can now put a new event together, and keep it as a draft until it is ready.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.071
The Events page lists every event, soonest first. Each row shows the date and time

00:00:13.071 --> 00:00:17.082
in Toronto, how many are going, and whether it is published.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.658
All, Published and Draft each show a count. A tab with nothing in it says so.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.201
New event opens the event editor at the side, with focus on the title. On a phone,

00:00:31.201 --> 00:00:32.769
it fills the screen.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.749
Save draft sends the event. While it waits, the button says Saving, and the fields

00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:41.686
hold still.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.571
Then the drawer closes, a toast says the draft is not visible to members yet, and

00:00:48.571 --> 00:00:49.887
the list shows it.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.000
With no events yet, the page offers the first one. If the list does not load, Try

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.349
again asks again.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.136
On the server, every field has its limits, and a refusal names each field's own

00:01:07.136 --> 00:01:10.751
code. The start must be after now, in Toronto time.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.922
Every test failed first. Now they all pass.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.624
Next, editing an event.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.979
That's slice ten point one. Christian Fitness: a Christian community for health in

00:01:28.979 --> 00:01:30.250
body and spirit.
